**F. `useListings` refetches on every mount** (`lib/useListings.ts`) - biggest win

Every navigation to Browse or Saved fires a full Supabase fetch. Add a module-level cache:

```typescript
let cachedListings: Listing[] | null = null;
let lastFetchTime = 0;
const CACHE_TTL = 5 * 60 * 1000;

export function useListings() {
  const [listings, setListings] = useState<Listing[]>(cachedListings ?? []);
  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(!cachedListings);

  const load = useCallback(async (forceRefresh = false) => {
    const now = Date.now();
    if (!forceRefresh && cachedListings && now - lastFetchTime < CACHE_TTL) {
      setListings(cachedListings);
      return;
    }
    setLoading(true);
    try {
      const data = await fetchListings();
      cachedListings = data;
      lastFetchTime = now;
      setListings(data);
    } finally {
      setLoading(false);
    }
  }, []);

  useEffect(() => { load(); }, [load]);
  return { listings, loading, refresh: () => load(true) };
}
```

**G. Expo Image cache policy** - wherever listing photos are displayed:

```typescript
<Image source={{ uri: photoUrl }} cachePolicy="memory-disk" />
```

---

The three animation/subscription patterns checked (OfflineBanner, Toast, Skeleton) **all have correct cleanup** - no leaks found there.

**H. Saved hook - all cards subscribe to full updates** (`lib/saved.ts:49-60`)

When a FlatList renders 20 cards, each calls `useSavedIds()` and adds a subscriber. Toggle any one save, and all 20 subscribers fire. Fix: make `useSaved(id)` subscribe only to its own ID's changes:

```typescript
export function useSaved(id: string): [boolean, () => boolean] {
  const [saved, setSaved] = useState(() => ids.includes(String(id)));

  useEffect(() => {
    const update = () => setSaved(ids.includes(String(id)));
    subs.add(update);
    ensureLoaded().then(update);
    return () => subs.delete(update);
  }, [id]);

  const toggle = useCallback(() => toggleSaved(id), [id]);
  return [saved, toggle];
}
```

---

**I. Admin stats object created inline every render** (`app/admin.tsx:56-63`)

```typescript
const stats = useMemo(() => {
  const sevenDaysAgo = Date.now() - 7 * 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000;
  return {
    total: listings.length,
    available: listings.filter((l) => l.status === 'available').length,
    claimed: listings.filter((l) => l.status === 'claimed').length,
    last7: listings.filter((l) => new Date(l.created_at).getTime() > sevenDaysAgo).length,
    photos: listings.reduce((s, l) => s + (l.photos?.length ?? 0), 0),
  };
}, [listings]);
```

**J. `countBy()` called 3x per render** (`app/admin.tsx:162-164`)

```typescript
const areaBreakdown    = useMemo(() => countBy(listings, 'area'), [listings]);
const subjectBreakdown = useMemo(() => countBy(listings, 'subject'), [listings]);
const gradeBreakdown   = useMemo(() => countBy(listings, 'grade_level'), [listings]);
```

